{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":501735,"name":"David G","username":"mason-feature-slayer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mason-feature-slayer/{size}/117249_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:52:17.240Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor IDE\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official 1Password Cursor plugin MCP server never connects. Cursor creates the client, then the shared MCP process fails while spawning the server:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConnection failed: spawn 1password-mcp EACCES\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe spawn policy log says sandboxed=false and sandboxReason=controls_disabled, so this is not the MCP sandbox blocking the process. The plugin mcp.json starts the bare command \u003ccode\u003e1password-mcp\u003c/code\u003e (no absolute path). The 1Password tools stay unavailable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall the 1Password plugin from the Cursor Marketplace (server id plugin-1password-1password).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e1Password desktop 8.12.36 is installed. The MCP binary inside the app is present and executable: /Applications/1Password.app/Contents/MacOS/1password-mcp (-rwxr-xr-x).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart Cursor, or reload MCP servers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn the MCP logs, createClient reports success, then stdio connect fails with spawn 1password-mcp EACCES.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFull log:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2026-09-26 11:39:35.010 [info] [MCPService] createClient: identifier=“plugin-1password-1password”, serverName=“1password”\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.012 [info] [MCPService] createClient completed for server: plugin-1password-1password, statusType=initializing, success=true\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.042 [info] [Shared MCP process] connecting stdio for “1password” (plugin-1password-1password)\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.042 [info] [Shared MCP process] [V2 FSM] connection:connect_start: conn=idle,auth=unknown → conn=connecting,auth=unknown\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.124 [info] [Shared MCP process] MCP stdio spawn policy decision: sandboxed=false, sandboxReason=controls_disabled, networkControlsEnabled=false, mcpNetworkMode=unset, mcpNetworkAllowlistCount=0, mcpNetworkDenylistCount=0, localAgentNetworkAllowlistCount=0, sandboxPolicyHash=dbad6ab7a53b8aaa3269e0c907d30e5e1483298ffc76de0456eeb31b7d11df5e\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.128 [warning] [Shared MCP process] Connection failed: spawn 1password-mcp EACCES\u003cbr\u003e\n2026-09-26 11:39:35.128 [warning] [Shared MCP process] [V2 FSM] connection:connect_failure: conn=connecting,auth=unknown → conn=failed,auth=unknown\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe 1Password plugin MCP server should start and expose its tools. The desktop app binary is executable, and the spawn log shows the sandbox is disabled, so the server should connect instead of failing with EACCES.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor IDE 3.22.7 (commit 37076c6c3f9e253c0fa2305197e45befd13a2260), arm64\u003cbr\u003e\nmacOS 27.0 (Build 26A428)\u003cbr\u003e\n1Password desktop 8.12.36\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal checks after the failure:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlugin mcp.json command is exactly “1password-mcp” with no args and no absolute path.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/Applications/1Password.app/Contents/MacOS/1password-mcp exists and is -rwxr-xr-x (owner dgitman:admin, about 4 MB, dated Sep 8). It has a Homebrew Cask quarantine xattr.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/usr/local/bin is drwx------ root:wheel (mtime Sep 21 15:45). The user cannot list it, and ls /usr/local/bin/1password-mcp returns Permission denied. That matches the EACCES from Cursor’s stdio spawn, which looks up 1password-mcp on PATH.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ewhich 1password-mcp does not find a usable command for this user.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRelated, different failure mode (Grok Bot, ENOENT, after a root-only /usr/local/bin/1password-mcp symlink): \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-cannot-spawn-1password-mcp-1password-mcp-enoent/168358\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot cannot spawn 1Password MCP (1password-mcp ENOENT)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-501735-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-501735-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-26T15:52:24.019Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":25.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173073,"topic_slug":"1password-plugin-mcp-fails-to-start-spawn-1password-mcp-eacces","display_username":"David G","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-cannot-spawn-1password-mcp-1password-mcp-enoent/168358","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot cannot spawn 1Password MCP (1password-mcp ENOENT)","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132182,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/1password-plugin-mcp-fails-to-start-spawn-1password-mcp-eacces/173073/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false}],"stream":[501735]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":47,"name":"mcp","slug":"mcp"},{"id":326,"name":"macos","slug":"macos"},{"id":372,"name":"plugins","slug":"plugins"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"1Password plugin MCP fails to start: spawn 1password-mcp EACCES","id":173073,"title":"1Password plugin MCP fails to start: spawn 1password-mcp EACCES","posts_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-26T15:52:17.176Z","views":14,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-26T15:52:17